wifi: iwlwifi: pcie: allocate a queue's entries with kvzalloc

iwl_pcie_txq_alloc() allocates a TX queue's entries array with
kzalloc, one struct iwl_pcie_txq_entry for each of its slots. With the
queue sizes newer devices use for a TID, that is 64 KiB to 128 KiB,
an order-4 or order-5 allocation, and the driver makes it each time it
adds a queue, as it does on joining an access point. On a machine whose
memory is fragmented, such an allocation is the first to fail, since
the page allocator doesn't retry past PAGE_ALLOC_COSTLY_ORDER:

  kworker/u67:5: page allocation failure: order:4,
    mode:0x40dc0(GFP_KERNEL|__GFP_ZERO|__GFP_COMP)
  Workqueue: events_unbound cfg80211_wiphy_work [cfg80211]
  ...
   __kmalloc_noprof+0x2a3/0x510
   iwl_pcie_txq_alloc+0xb0/0x2e0 [iwlwifi]
   iwl_txq_dyn_alloc_dma+0xb8/0x170 [iwlwifi]
   iwl_txq_dyn_alloc+0xfe/0x3d0 [iwlwifi]
  iwlwifi 0000:00:14.3: Tx queue alloc failed

The association then fails, here roaming between two access points of
a mesh on a BE211 with 64 GB of memory, a third of it free.

Only the CPU reads the entries array; the device reads the TFDs and the
first TB buffers, which dma_alloc_coherent() allocates apart. So the
array needn't be physically contiguous. Allocate it with kvzalloc, which
falls back to vmalloc when no contiguous block is free, and free it with
kvfree everywhere it is freed.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/gen1_2/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/gen1_2/tx.c
@@ -468,7 +468,7 @@ static void iwl_pcie_txq_free(struct iwl
 				  txq->first_tb_bufs, txq->first_tb_dma);
 	}
 
-	kfree(txq->entries);
+	kvfree(txq->entries);
 	txq->entries = NULL;
 
 	timer_delete_sync(&txq->stuck_timer);
@@ -741,7 +741,7 @@ int iwl_pcie_txq_alloc(struct iwl_trans
 
 	txq->n_window = slots_num;
 
-	txq->entries = kzalloc_objs(struct iwl_pcie_txq_entry, slots_num);
+	txq->entries = kvzalloc_objs(struct iwl_pcie_txq_entry, slots_num);
 
 	if (!txq->entries)
 		goto error;
@@ -789,7 +789,7 @@ error:
 	if (txq->entries && cmd_queue)
 		for (i = 0; i < slots_num; i++)
 			kfree(txq->entries[i].cmd);
-	kfree(txq->entries);
+	kvfree(txq->entries);
 	txq->entries = NULL;
 
 	return -ENOMEM;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/gen1_2/tx-gen2.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/gen1_2/tx-gen2.c
@@ -867,7 +867,7 @@ static void iwl_txq_gen2_free_memory(str
 				  txq->first_tb_bufs, txq->first_tb_dma);
 	}
 
-	kfree(txq->entries);
+	kvfree(txq->entries);
 	if (txq->bc_tbl.addr)
 		dma_pool_free(trans_pcie->txqs.bc_pool,
 			      txq->bc_tbl.addr, txq->bc_tbl.dma);
